WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.867 --> 00:00:16.988
There was no possibility of taking a walk that day.

2
00:00:18.068 --> 00:00:24.070
The cold November wind had brought so much rain that outdoor exercise was out of the question.

3
00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:31.692
My cousins, Eliza, John, and Georgiana Reed, were clustered around their mama in the sitting room.

4
00:00:32.904 --> 00:00:36.088
For the moment they were neither quarreling nor crying.

5
00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:43.658
Mrs. Reed looked perfectly happy as she reclined on a sofa by the fireside with her darlings around

6
00:00:43.718 --> 00:00:47.322
her. She had excluded me from the group.

7
00:00:47.342 --> 00:00:51.788
"I hate to keep you at a distance, Jane," she said.

8
00:00:52.968 --> 00:00:58.971
"But until I hear from the nurse or learn from my own observations that you are honestly trying

9
00:00:59.011 --> 00:01:06.094
to acquire a better disposition, I must exclude you from privileges intended only for happy children."

10
00:01:06.114 --> 00:01:08.995
"What does the nurse say I've done?"

11
00:01:09.475 --> 00:01:10.036
I asked.

12
00:01:11.156 --> 00:01:14.097
"Jane, I don't like children who ask questions.

13
00:01:15.238 --> 00:01:20.020
Be seated somewhere and remain silent until you can speak pleasantly."

14
00:01:21.788 --> 00:01:23.970
A small room adjoined the sitting room.

15
00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:28.553
I slipped in there and soon picked out a book from the bookcase.

16
00:01:29.654 --> 00:01:33.716
Climbing onto the window seat, I drew the curtain closed around me.

17
00:01:34.877 --> 00:01:40.441
I feared nothing except interruption, and that came too soon when the door opened.

18
00:01:40.461 --> 00:01:43.183
"Boo!" cried John.

19
00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:46.946
Then he paused because the room seemed empty.

20
00:01:46.966 --> 00:01:50.068
"Eliza! Georgiana!"

21
00:01:50.472 --> 00:01:51.893
he called to his sisters.

22
00:01:51.913 --> 00:01:54.115
"Jane isn't here.

23
00:01:55.215 --> 00:01:57.677
Tell Mama she has run out into the rain."

24
00:01:58.898 --> 00:02:05.562
John never would have found me, but Eliza looked into the room and said at once, "She's in

25
00:02:05.642 --> 00:02:07.003
the window seat, John."

26
00:02:08.164 --> 00:02:13.127
I came out immediately because I trembled at the idea of John dragging me out.

27
00:02:13.147 --> 00:02:15.048
"What do you want?"

28
00:02:15.549 --> 00:02:16.129
I asked.

29
00:02:16.149 --> 00:02:20.052
"Say, 'What do you want, Master Reed?'"

30
00:02:20.468 --> 00:02:21.268
he replied.

31
00:02:21.288 --> 00:02:24.010
"I want you to come here."

32
00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:30.332
Seating himself in an armchair, he motioned for me to stand before him.

33
00:02:31.473 --> 00:02:35.434
John was a 14-year-old schoolboy while I was only 10.

34
00:02:36.535 --> 00:02:43.197
He bullied me constantly, but his mother never noticed, and the servants didn't like to offend him by

35
00:02:43.257 --> 00:02:44.378
taking my side.

36
00:02:45.578 --> 00:02:49.620
I approached John, and he spent three minutes sticking out his tongue at me.

37
00:02:50.792 --> 00:02:54.294
All at once he hit me so hard that I staggered back.

38
00:02:54.314 --> 00:02:59.596
"That's for your impudence in answering Mama a while ago," he said.

39
00:02:59.616 --> 00:03:02.657
"And for sneaking behind the curtain."

40
00:03:03.057 --> 00:03:06.779
Accustomed to his abuse, I had no intention of replying.

41
00:03:07.919 --> 00:03:11.761
My main concern was how to endure the blow that would surely follow.

42
00:03:11.781 --> 00:03:14.682
"What were you doing behind the curtain?"

43
00:03:15.082 --> 00:03:15.802
John asked.

44
00:03:16.903 --> 00:03:19.324
"Reading." "Show me the book."

45
00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.602
I returned to the window seat and fetched it for him.

46
00:03:23.622 --> 00:03:26.764
"You have no business taking our books.

47
00:03:28.045 --> 00:03:31.228
Mama says your father left you no money," said John.

48
00:03:31.248 --> 00:03:37.873
"You ought to be out begging, not living here with gentlemen's children like us, eating our food and

49
00:03:37.913 --> 00:03:39.954
wearing clothes at our mother's expense.

50
00:03:41.155 --> 00:03:43.337
I'll teach you not to rummage through my bookshelves.

51
00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:47.660
Go stand by the door, away from the mirror and windows."

52
00:03:48.964 --> 00:03:54.166
I puzzled over those last directions until I saw him ready to hurl the book at me.

53
00:03:55.406 --> 00:03:57.887
I darted aside, but it was too late.

54
00:03:59.047 --> 00:04:02.908
The book hit me, and I fell against the door, cutting my head.

55
00:04:02.928 --> 00:04:05.649
"Wicked and cruel boy!"

56
00:04:06.049 --> 00:04:06.649
I shouted.

57
00:04:06.669 --> 00:04:12.511
"You are like a murderer, a slave driver—" "What did you say?"

58
00:04:12.931 --> 00:04:13.531
he cried.

59
00:04:13.551 --> 00:04:21.647
"I'll tell Mama, but first—" John ran headlong at me, grasping my hair and shoulder.

60
00:04:23.368 --> 00:04:27.430
I don't remember what I did to him, but he bellowed, and Mrs.

61
00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:30.252
Reed came running, followed by two servants.

62
00:04:31.512 --> 00:04:33.814
"How could you fly at Master John like that?"

63
00:04:34.234 --> 00:04:35.575
said Bessie, the nurse.

64
00:04:35.595 --> 00:04:39.918
"Did anybody ever see such a picture of passion?"

65
00:04:40.338 --> 00:04:42.359
said Miss Abbot, who was Mrs.

66
00:04:42.459 --> 00:04:43.720
Reed's personal maid.

67
00:04:44.896 --> 00:04:47.538
"Take her away to the red room and lock her in!"

68
00:04:47.938 --> 00:04:48.619
ordered Mrs.

69
00:04:48.699 --> 00:04:54.182
Reed. I resisted all the way upstairs, something new for me.

70
00:04:54.202 --> 00:04:56.244
"For shame!"

71
00:04:56.624 --> 00:04:57.625
cried Miss Abbot.

72
00:04:58.645 --> 00:05:03.869
"What shocking conduct, Miss Jane, to strike a young gentleman, your young master."

73
00:05:03.889 --> 00:05:06.390
"How is he my master?"

74
00:05:06.791 --> 00:05:10.613
I asked, still struggling against them as we reached the red room.

75
00:05:10.633 --> 00:05:12.815
"Am I a servant?"

76
00:05:14.055 --> 00:05:19.660
"No, you are less than a servant because you do nothing for your keep," said Miss Abbot.

77
00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:23.582
"Sit down and think over your wickedness."

78
00:05:24.703 --> 00:05:28.526
"You ought to be aware, miss, that you are under obligation to Mrs.

79
00:05:28.586 --> 00:05:29.987
Reed," said Bessie.

80
00:05:30.007 --> 00:05:35.951
"If she were to turn you out from Gateshead Hall, you'd have to go to the poorhouse."

81
00:05:37.212 --> 00:05:38.413
I had nothing to say.

82
00:05:38.433 --> 00:05:45.802
"If you don't repent," said Miss Abbot, "something bad might be permitted to come down the chimney and

83
00:05:45.902 --> 00:05:46.882
fetch you away."

84
00:05:48.083 --> 00:05:51.884
Then they went out, shutting the door and locking it behind them.

85
00:05:52.945 --> 00:05:58.147
The red room was a spare bedroom, very seldom used despite its large size.

86
00:05:59.387 --> 00:06:05.470
Mr. Reed had died in this room nine years ago, and since then few people had crossed its

87
00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:09.772
threshold. I sat on a low ottoman near the fireplace.

88
00:06:10.912 --> 00:06:12.693
Why could I never please anyone?

89
00:06:13.774 --> 00:06:17.175
Eliza, who was headstrong and selfish, was respected.

90
00:06:18.316 --> 00:06:22.838
Georgiana, who had a spoiled temperament, was always indulged.

91
00:06:23.979 --> 00:06:28.061
My head still ached and bled from the blow I'd received from John.

92
00:06:29.762 --> 00:06:31.323
Why did no one punish him?

93
00:06:32.484 --> 00:06:38.127
I knew if I were a happy, handsome, romping child, everyone would treat me better.

94
00:06:39.207 --> 00:06:43.354
It was past four o'clock, and daylight began to fade from the red room.

95
00:06:44.595 --> 00:06:47.938
Rain beat on the windows and wind howled in the trees.

96
00:06:49.079 --> 00:06:50.520
I started to think of Mr.

97
00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:52.362
Reed, my mother's brother.

98
00:06:53.503 --> 00:06:56.945
He had taken me in when I was an infant without parents.

99
00:06:58.186 --> 00:07:00.729
In his last moments, he'd made Mrs.

100
00:07:00.809 --> 00:07:04.111
Reed promise to rear me as one of her own children.

101
00:07:05.272 --> 00:07:09.456
I never doubted that my uncle would have treated me kindly if he'd lived.

102
00:07:10.548 --> 00:07:16.271
Then I began to recall stories I'd heard about dead men, troubled by the violation of their last

103
00:07:16.331 --> 00:07:20.314
wishes. Suddenly a light gleamed on the wall.

104
00:07:21.474 --> 00:07:24.736
I shrieked and rushed to the door, desperately pounding on it.

105
00:07:25.857 --> 00:07:27.678
Bessie and Miss Abbot came running.

106
00:07:27.698 --> 00:07:30.660
"Why are you screaming?"

107
00:07:31.100 --> 00:07:32.741
asked Bessie, opening the door.

108
00:07:32.761 --> 00:07:34.602
"Let me out!"

109
00:07:35.002 --> 00:07:35.502
I cried.

110
00:07:35.522 --> 00:07:38.004
"I think I saw a ghost!"

111
00:07:39.168 --> 00:07:43.250
"I know the girl's naughty tricks," Miss Abbot said in disgust.

112
00:07:44.391 --> 00:07:45.272
"What's all this?"

113
00:07:45.752 --> 00:07:46.612
demanded Mrs.

114
00:07:46.692 --> 00:07:48.553
Reed, walking into the room.

115
00:07:48.573 --> 00:07:52.756
"I said Jane was to stay here alone."

116
00:07:52.776 --> 00:07:57.898
"But she screamed so loud," pleaded Bessie, holding my hand.

117
00:07:57.918 --> 00:08:01.500
"I despise trickery," said Mrs.

118
00:08:01.581 --> 00:08:04.922
Reed. "You will stay here an extra hour."

119
00:08:04.942 --> 00:08:09.441
"Oh, Aunt, have pity, let me—" "Silence!"

120
00:08:09.881 --> 00:08:10.721
commanded Mrs.

121
00:08:10.781 --> 00:08:15.964
Reed. Ignoring my wild sobs, she abruptly locked me in again.

122
00:08:17.105 --> 00:08:22.328
I heard her walking away, and then, dear reader, I soon lost consciousness.
